# What NOT to ship in the published package. The package.json "files" field is the PRIMARY control — an allowlist,
# so nothing ships unless it is listed there. This denylist is defense-in-depth: it trims development-only material
# out of the allowlisted lib/ tree, and it names the sensitive files explicitly so they stay excluded even if the
# allowlist is ever loosened.

# Development-only material within lib/ (tests, dev scripts) and the dev hooks/docs
lib/test/
lib/scripts/
.githooks/
docs/BACKLOG.md
docs/TEAM-VAULTS-DESIGN.md
docs/SECURITY.md
docs/THIRD-PARTY-LICENSES.md
virtual-disk-backlog.md

# Secrets and release-signing material — MUST NEVER ship (the private key is the whole trust root)
release-signing-key.json
release-manifest.json
release-manifest.sig
SHA256SUMS
SHA256SUMS.sig

# Runtime data, the test scratch tree, and the downloaded engine — created on a machine, never shipped
data/
.test-data/
node_modules/
package-lock.json

# OS cruft
.DS_Store
